    "deletePage" ["Delete a page" (str "Deletes one page through Logseq's page deletion rules, including its block tree: the page moves to the Recycle bin and links to it become plain text. Today's journal is the exception, as in the app: its blocks are deleted and the page is kept. " today-note " A journal is refused with 500 while the TIMEZONE setting names an unknown zone. Refuses with 409 and deletes nothing while other blocks or pages reference it (link to it, embed it, alias it or hold it as a property value), unless acknowledge-references is true; the error gives the count. Pass dry-run=true to get the counts without deleting, with the page under affected: its references, its block count (blocks) and the first line of its first three top-level blocks (roots). A delete answers 200 naming the page (affected); on today's journal it also answers truncated: true and the number of blocks deleted (cleared), and its dry run answers truncated: true. A page still there afterwards answers 500 naming it in the error and under not-removed.")]
